{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430268-vtm5-banu-haqim-clan-compulsion","id":1430268,"title":"[VtM5] Banu Haqim clan compulsion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-28T14:37:22-08:00","id":1430268,"title":"[VtM5] Banu Haqim clan compulsion","content":"On page 166 of the Camarilla book for VtM5 it states:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>For one scene, the vampire must slake at least one Hunger from anyone, friend or foe, that acts against a<br /> Conviction of theirs. Failing to do so results in a three-dice penalty to all rolls until the Compulsion is satisfied<br /> or the scene ends. (If the one fed from is also a vampire, don\u2019t forget to test for Bane-induced Hunger frenzy.)</i><br /> </div> Does that mean that the character basically has to kill any mortal that acts against a character's Conviction if their Hunger is low, since that's the only way to reduce Hunger to 0 for a Vampire with a sufficiently high Blood Potency<i>? </i>What happens if Hunger is already at 0?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1577-maledicta","user":"Maledicta","date":". 12-28-2020, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1577-maledicta","name":"Maledicta","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T20:48:19-08:00","id":1430308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maledicta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430268-vtm5-banu-haqim-clan-compulsion#post1430268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... What happens if Hunger is already at 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>If their Hunger is already at 0 then they cannot roll a Bestial Failure or Messy Critical and get a compulsion unless someone used Dementation and does enough Willpower damage to impair them. A let's face it, if you give someone the Banu compulsion from Dementation you deserve the impending bite from said Banu that is likely coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T01:18:06-08:00","id":1430316,"title":"","content":"It does not imply killing a mortal, the resolution is to satisfy one hunger of the &quot;offender&quot; be it mortal or vampire - also you can decide to not follow the compulsion, but suffer the penality.<br /> Compulsion are like an itch - it feels good to follow them - i.e. getting rid of the penalities.<br /> <br /> Slaking one Hunger is not the same as reducing the Hunger score by 1. Even a Vamp at Hunger 0 can slake 1 Hunger (but can nothing do with it)<br /> <br /> Btw: I would rather house rule make the Penality = Bane Severity (Which would be -2 for a BP 1 Banu Haqim), this would fit in nicer with the general design of the penality driven compulsions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T17:28:37-08:00","id":1430395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430268-vtm5-banu-haqim-clan-compulsion?p=1430316#post1430316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not imply killing a mortal, the resolution is to satisfy one hunger of the &quot;offender&quot; be it mortal or vampire - also you can decide to not follow the compulsion, but suffer the penality.<br /> Compulsion are like an itch - it feels good to follow them - i.e. getting rid of the penalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still, it's pretty harsh compared to the other clans' compulsions, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Slaking one Hunger is not the same as reducing the Hunger score by 1. Even a Vamp at Hunger 0 can slake 1 Hunger (but can nothing do with it) </div> </div> </div>That's very vague and abstract, imo. But I get what you're saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Btw: I would rather house rule make the Penality = Bane Severity (Which would be -2 for a BP 1 Banu Haqim), this would fit in nicer with the general design of the penality driven compulsions. </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea, I'll probably do that.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1577-maledicta","name":"Maledicta","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}